{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":2423078,"ns":0,"title":"Admissible numbering","extract":"In computability theory, admissible numberings are enumerations (numberings) of the set of partial computable functions that can be converted to and from the standard numbering of partial computable functions. These numberings are also called acceptable numberings and acceptable programming systems.","description":"Concept in computability theory","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}